      "sourceTextSha256": "8ffdd3c90b01fc8ff2830935baf72f0486bf5a876d07b1bc1e0ca6edb77ac7e7",
      "text": "Day 4 · A day to relax and get to know the town: a boat tour of Paraty Bay, visiting beautiful beaches and islands, with lunch on one of the islands, and in the evening a tour of the historic centre. The small coastal town of Paraty, a UNESCO World Heritage Site, is like a museum in a tropical setting, with one of the finest collections of 18th-century Portuguese colonial buildings. In the 1700s, gold from Minas Gerais was carried through the mountains to Paraty and shipped to Portugal; when a better route via Rio was found, the town kept its original charm.",
